  "$spectrum": "Hue ramps. Twelve are defined so any stored value always renders, but only eight ship as the palette: rose, amber, citron, fern, teal, sky, indigo, violet. Those eight are evenly spread and are what auto-assignment draws from. Twelve read as a paint chart, and the four held back sat too close to their neighbours to tell apart at a glance, which is the only thing a hue is for here. The October 2026 redesign came back with amber, citron and fern text a little lighter than these; see docs/redesign/README.md. The values here are darker and clear 4.5:1 on white with room, so they stay. 100 tints an area, 500 is the identity, 700 is text-safe, 900 pairs for dark, and sits above the dark card rather than under it: a tint darker than the surface it is drawn on is a bar nobody can see.",
